| **Gross yield** | **3.40%** |

---

### Net Yield (1.5% maintenance assumption)
| Deduction | Amount (p.a.) |
|---|---|
| Maintenance / MCST (1.5% × $2.4M) | –$36,000 |
| Net rental income | $45,600 |
| **Net yield** | **1.90%** |

---

### Net Yield (with property tax added)
| Deduction | Amount (p.a.) |
|---|---|
| Maintenance (1.5%) | –$36,000 |
| IRAS property tax (NOO progressive rate est.) | –$18,576 |
| Net rental income | ~$27,024 |
| **Net yield (full holding costs)** | **~1.13%** |

---

### Advisor Flags

1. **Verify the 1.5% maintenance figure.** At $36,000/year, this is high for pure MCST fees on a single unit. If it's meant to proxy *all* holding costs (MCST + property tax + vacancy), re-label it accordingly — don't double-count.

2. **Property tax is the big surprise.** At NOO progressive rates, estimated IRAS tax is ~$18,576/year. Many clients don't anticipate this until the first bill — surface it early.

3. **This is a cap-gains play, not a yield play.** At ~1.1% net unlevered yield, the property will likely run negative carry if financed. Run a cashflow stress test before the client commits — especially with SORA-based packages currently above 3%.


